# Binary demo media → Git LFS.
# Keeps the .git history light on every re-encode (a ~16 MB pair of mp4
# walkthroughs was previously committed as plain blobs). New media matching
# these patterns is automatically stored in LFS; clones fetch on demand.
# NOTE: this converts FUTURE + newly-staged additions. The two demo mp4s are
# re-staged as LFS pointers; shrinking already-pushed history requires a
# separate BFG / git-filter-repo pass (not done here).
*.mp4  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.webm filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mov  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
